-- title:
--   Commute GHalf Sandwich Error Mono Length
-- statement:
--   **The half-sandwich commutation error is monotone in its length.**
--
--   Let $(m,q,d)$ be LDT parameters, let $\gamma,\zeta\ge0$, and let $j,k\in\mathbb N$ satisfy $j\le k$. Define
--
--   $$
--   E(r)=426r^2m\left(\gamma^{1/16}+\zeta^{1/16}+(d/q)^{1/16}\right).
--   $$
--
--   Then the displayed half-sandwich error is monotone:
--
--   $$
--   E(j)\le E(k).
--   $$
--
--   The nonnegative error factor is independent of the length, so this is the quadratic monotonicity step used to replace a shorter half-sandwich estimate by the estimate at the full length in the from-H-to-G head-tail bound.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
